Calibration:
  A first real-TiKV run inherited realtikvtest ManagedLockTTL=5000ms. The reader
  rolled back the lock instead of pushing minCommitTS, so that run was invalid as
  a product verdict. Restoring the production client-go default 20000ms and using
  a 4 MiB write produced a ~12s primary lock and the natural RED above.

Production equivalence:
  The harness stops renewal and holds the first Commit only to compress a writer-
  local pause. A node-specific TiDB-to-TiKV/PD interruption, long GC/runtime pause,
  severe CPU starvation, or OS scheduling stall longer than 5s has the same owner
  effect while a second TiDB remains healthy. TiKV generated the lock resolution,
  minCommitTS push, CommitTsExpired response, retry outcome, and fresh read state.
